From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_port: discard RX physical errors in BMI (vendor parity)

Under full-rate VLAN<->untagged bidir traffic the mEMAC RX FIFOs
overflow. That is a hardware limit of this traffic mix, and the vendor
stack does it too, at more than twice the rate on .106 (2026-10-05). ASK2
enqueued every such frame (FM_FD_ERR_PHYSICAL) to the port error FQ, so
the kernel processed and logged ~26K error frames/s per port ("Err FD
status = 0x00080000", ratelimited) exactly when the box was saturated.
The vendor discards them in BMI (FMBM_RFSDM 0x010ee3c0).

Add FM_PORT_FRM_ERR_PHYSICAL to the default RX discard mask. The frame
was lost anyway; the drop stays visible in the mEMAC rdrp/rerr counters.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index 601767e..43469df 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -55,7 +55,13 @@
 
 #define DFLT_PORT_CUT_BYTES_FROM_END		4
 
-#define DFLT_PORT_ERRORS_TO_DISCARD		FM_PORT_FRM_ERR_CLS_DISCARD
+/* Physical errors (MAC RX FIFO overflow under load) are discarded in BMI,
+ * as the vendor SDK does (FMBM_RFSDM 0x010ee3c0 on .106), instead of being
+ * enqueued to the error FQ where dpaa_rx_error() logs and counts each one.
+ * The frame is lost either way; the mEMAC rdrp/rerr counters still record it.
+ */
+#define DFLT_PORT_ERRORS_TO_DISCARD		(FM_PORT_FRM_ERR_CLS_DISCARD | \
+						 FM_PORT_FRM_ERR_PHYSICAL)
 #define DFLT_PORT_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH		9600
 
 #define DFLT_PORT_RX_FIFO_PRI_ELEVATION_LEV(bmi_max_fifo_size)	\
